Module194202Name = AuVo E-Rechnung
Module194202Desc = E-invoices for Dolibarr (ZUGFeRD / Factur-X EN16931)

AuvoERechnungSetup = AuVo E-Rechnung setup
AuvoERechnungBankAccount = Bank account (IBAN/BIC)
AuvoERechnungPaymentMeans = Default payment means
AuvoERechnungPaymentMeansHint = UNTDID 4461 code. 30/58 (credit transfer) require an IBAN: without a configured bank account, the payment means block is omitted from the XML (BR-61). 59 (SEPA direct debit) publishes the creditor ICS (Dolibarr constant PRELEVEMENT_ICS), the mandate reference and the IBAN of the third party's default bank account.
PaymentMeans30 = Credit transfer
PaymentMeans58 = SEPA credit transfer
PaymentMeans59 = SEPA direct debit
PaymentMeans49 = Direct debit (national)
AuvoERechnungBrCheck = EN16931 business rules check
AuvoERechnungBrCheckHint = Checks a subset of the EN16931 Schematron rules before injection (BR-CO-10..17, BR-27, BR-61, BR-IC-11/12, VAT category consistency...). Violations block in strict mode, otherwise they are added to the warnings.
AuvoERechnungVeraPdfPath = PDF/A-3 validation with veraPDF (optional, external tool)
AuvoERechnungVeraPdfPathHint = Empty by default = disabled, and that's fine: the EN16931 XSD check and internal BR rules already run. veraPDF is NOT shipped with the module — it's a third-party tool you install yourself (https://verapdf.org), then point to here. If set, every PDF is re-validated as PDF/A-3b after injection: non blocking (a failure just adds a warning), slows generation by a few seconds.
AuvoERechnungVeraPdfPlaceholder = e.g. /usr/local/bin/verapdf — empty = disabled
AuvoERechnungInfo = Generated PDF invoices will automatically be converted to Factur-X EN16931 (PDF/A-3 with embedded CrossIndustryInvoice XML). IBAN and BIC are read from the selected bank account.
AuvoERechnungDiagTitle = Mandatory information diagnostic
AuvoERechnungDiagResults = Factur-X EN16931 + BR-FR rules check
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerName = Seller company name
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerAddress = Seller address
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerVAT = Intra-community VAT number
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerVATFranchise = not required (French VAT franchise, art. 293 B CGI) — the SIREN is published as tax identifier
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerSIRET = SIRET / SIREN
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerSteuernummer = Seller tax number (BT-32)
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerSteuernummerNotNeeded = not set — not required, VAT ID present
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerTaxIdMissing = Seller tax number or VAT ID missing — one of them is mandatory (BR-CO-26)
AuvoERechnungDiagSellerEmail = Seller email
AuvoERechnungDiagIBAN = Bank account IBAN
AuvoERechnungDiagBIC = Bank account BIC
AuvoERechnungDiagBankNotFound = Bank account not found
AuvoERechnungDiagBankNotSet = No bank account selected
AuvoERechnungDiagModuleBankEnabled = Bank module enabled
AuvoERechnungDiagModuleBankDisabled = Bank module disabled (required to manage the bank account)
AuvoERechnungDiagModuleInvoiceEnabled = Invoice module enabled
AuvoERechnungDiagModuleInvoiceDisabled = Invoice module disabled (required to generate invoices)
AuvoERechnungDiagForceFontOk = Embedded PDF font forced (MAIN_PDF_FORCE_FONT)
AuvoERechnungDiagForceFontMissing = MAIN_PDF_FORCE_FONT not set — without embedded fonts, the PDF is not PDF/A-3 compliant
AuvoERechnungDiagInjInProcess = In-process injection (no exec) forced — works on servers where exec() is disabled
AuvoERechnungDiagInjAuto = Automatic mode: subprocess injection (exec available) — isolated PHP process, the safest path
AuvoERechnungDiagInjAutoNoExec = Automatic mode: in-process injection (exec disabled on this server — no alternative available)
AuvoERechnungDiagInjSubprocess = Subprocess injection (exec) — legacy mode forced
AuvoERechnungDiagExecRequiredSub = "Subprocess" mode selected but exec() is disabled on this server — switch to "Automatic" or "In-process" in the configuration
AuvoERechnungDiagTcpdiConflict = In-process injection will fail: Dolibarr loads its "tcpdi" PDF engine on every generation (a TCPDF-based FPDF, incompatible with the Factur-X injection library). Two solutions: enable the exec() function on the server (the module then uses an isolated subprocess, recommended), OR set the constant MAIN_DISABLE_TCPDI = 1 (unblocks in-process, but disables Dolibarr's PDF merge features — page backgrounds, concatenation).
AuvoERechnungErrTcpdiConflict = FPDF/TCPDF conflict: Dolibarr loaded its tcpdi engine (%s), incompatible with in-process injection. Enable exec() (subprocess mode) or set the MAIN_DISABLE_TCPDI=1 constant (disables Dolibarr PDF merging).
AuvoERechnungDiagPhpCliOk = PHP CLI binary
AuvoERechnungDiagPhpCliNotFound = The configured PHP CLI binary cannot be found or is not executable: %s
AuvoERechnungDiagMulticurrencyNote = Multicurrency module enabled: invoices in a foreign currency are NOT converted to Factur-X (documented limitation, the classic PDF is kept)
AuvoERechnungDiagFixLink = Fix
AuvoERechnungDiagFixForceFont = Fix automatically (sets "pdfahelvetica")
AuvoERechnungForceFontSet = MAIN_PDF_FORCE_FONT set to "pdfahelvetica": generated PDFs now embed fonts (PDF/A-3). Global setting, applied to every PDF document in Dolibarr.
AuvoERechnungDiagAllOk = All mandatory information is filled in!
AuvoERechnungDiagNoBlocker = No blocker: Factur-X compliance is ensured. A few recommended items remain (in orange) you may address for an optimal result.

AuvoERechnungStrictMode = Error handling mode
AuvoERechnungStrictModeHint = Best-effort: if Factur-X generation fails, the classic PDF is delivered with a warning. Strict: blocks generation with a visible error if the XML is invalid or the PDF injection fails. Note: even in strict mode, the classic PDF already generated by Dolibarr remains on disk.
AuvoERechnungStrictModeBestEffort = Best-effort (default, non blocking)
AuvoERechnungStrictModeStrict = Strict (blocks if Factur-X fails)
AuvoERechnungInjectionMode = XML injection mode
AuvoERechnungInjectionModeHint = "Automatic" (recommended): subprocess if exec() is available (the safest, isolated path), and in-process only if exec() is disabled (hardened shared hosting). "In-process only" forces injection without exec() — reserve it for servers without exec(), since a PDF library conflict with another module can then prevent injection. "Subprocess" forces the legacy behaviour (requires exec()).
AuvoERechnungInjectionModeAuto = Automatic (subprocess if exec, otherwise in-process)
AuvoERechnungInjectionModeInProcess = In-process only (no exec)
AuvoERechnungInjectionModeSubprocess = Subprocess (exec, legacy)
AuvoERechnungPhpCliPath = PHP CLI binary path
AuvoERechnungPhpCliPathHint = Used only by the "subprocess" mode. Leave empty: the module auto-detects the right PHP CLI binary. Set a path only to force a specific binary (exotic setup).
AuvoERechnungLegalNotes = Mandatory French legal mentions (BR-FR-05)
AuvoERechnungNotePMD = Late payment penalties (PMD)
AuvoERechnungNotePMT = Recovery indemnity (PMT)
AuvoERechnungNoteAAB = Early payment discount (AAB)
AuvoERechnungLegalNotesForeignHint = Seller established outside France: no default mention is applied (the default texts come from the French Commercial Code). Fields left empty produce no note in the XML — enter your own mentions here if your national law requires them.

